<+># Week 5 - Data Structures\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Assignments:\r\n* [Hello](https://cs50.harvard.edu/x/psets/6/hello/)\r\n    - Implement a hello world program in Python.\r\n* [Mario (more)](https://cs50.harvard.edu/x/psets/6/mario/more/)\r\n    - Implement a program that prints out a pyramid of a specified height, implemented in Python.\r\n* [Cash](https://cs50.harvard.edu/x/psets/6/cash/)\r\n    - Implement a program that calculates the minimum number of coins needed to make change for a given amount of money, implemented in Python.\r\n* [Credit](https://cs50.harvard.edu/x/psets/6/credit/)\r\n    - Implement a program that validates credit card numbers and identifies the type of card, implemented in Python.\r\n* [Readability](https://cs50.harvard.edu/x/psets/6/readability/)\r\n    - Implement a program that calculates the approximate grade level needed to comprehend a given text, implemented in Python.\r\n* [DNA](https://cs50.harvard.edu/x/psets/6/dna/)\r\n    - Implement a program that identifies a person based on their DNA sequence, implemented in Python.\r\n
